class.description:
[SeedServer] holds one [member global_seed]. Named random streams ([RandomNumberGenerator]) and noise generators (such as [FastNoiseLite]) derive their own seeds from it, so that each system of a game draws from its own stream and does not change the numbers of another system. The same global seed gives the same numbers on every platform, in GDScript, C# and GDExtension. This is useful for procedural worlds, replays, daily challenges and tests.
The seed of a stream is derived from [member global_seed] and the stream's name with fixed hashes (FNV-1a 64 over the UTF-8 bytes of the name, mixed with SplitMix64). Unlike [method String.hash], these values do not change between engine versions.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
SeedServer.set_seed_from_text("Daily-2026-11-23")
var loot = SeedServer.get_rng("loot")
var weather = SeedServer.get_rng("weather")
print(loot.randi_range(1, 6)) # Always the same number for this text.

# Save the state with the save game ...
var state = SeedServer.get_state()
# ... and restore it later: the streams continue exactly where they were.
SeedServer.set_state(state)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
SeedServer.SetSeedFromText("Daily-2026-11-23");
RandomNumberGenerator loot = SeedServer.GetRng("loot");
RandomNumberGenerator weather = SeedServer.GetRng("weather");
GD.Print(loot.RandiRange(1, 6)); // Always the same number for this text.

// Save the state with the save game ...
Godot.Collections.Dictionary state = SeedServer.GetState();
// ... and restore it later: the streams continue exactly where they were.
SeedServer.SetState(state);
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] The methods of [SeedServer] are thread-safe. A single [RandomNumberGenerator] is not: use each stream from one thread only, or give each thread its own stream (for example [code]"worker_%d" % index[/code]).
[b]Note:[/b] The numbers of a stream depend on the algorithm of [RandomNumberGenerator] (PCG32). If a future engine version changes that algorithm, the derived seeds stay the same, but the drawn numbers may differ.
